{
  "summary": "The previous proposal is solid on the mechanical implementation but has several gaps worth addressing. First, the proposal says to inject the ideation_prompt 'above the role instructions' as a top-level directive, but this creates a tension: the ideating.md template already has a structured flow (description -> task -> role -> discussion), and inserting a user directive above the role instruction could confuse the LLM about whether it should follow the role (e.g., 'critique the previous proposal') or defer to the user's seed prompt — there needs to be clear prompt hierarchy language like 'The following user direction takes precedence over default role instructions where they conflict.' Second, the proposal doesn't address what happens to the ideation_prompt field after ideation completes — should it be auto-cleared so the next ideation run doesn't re-use stale seeds, or preserved so the user can see what direction they gave? The user's description suggests they want to set it when re-sending items through ideation, implying it should probably persist for reference but be ignorable, with a UI indicator showing 'this item has a seed prompt' so users know to clear or update it. Third, the proposal mentions a new API endpoint 'edit-ideation-prompt' in api.go, but the existing edit flow already handles arbitrary field updates — adding a dedicated endpoint is unnecessary complexity when the generic edit endpoint could simply accept ideation_prompt as another editable field, consistent with how description and other fields are already edited."
}
